Here is a complete explanation of how to add a custom OpenAPI extension to a specific path operation in FastAPI:

---

## Adding a Custom OpenAPI Extension to a Path Operation

FastAPI provides the `openapi_extra` parameter on path operation decorators as a low-level extension point for customizing the OpenAPI schema of individual operations. [https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/path-operation-advanced-configuration/]

---

### How It Works

When you declare a path operation, FastAPI automatically generates the relevant metadata (tags, parameters, requestBody, responses, etc.) to be included in the OpenAPI schema. [https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/path-operation-advanced-configuration/] You can **extend** this auto-generated schema using the `openapi_extra` parameter. [https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/path-operation-advanced-configuration/]

---

### Basic Example: Adding an OpenAPI Extension Field

OpenAPI extensions are custom fields prefixed with `x-`. You simply pass them as key-value pairs inside `openapi_extra`:

```python
from fastapi import FastAPI

app = FastAPI()

@app.get("/items/", openapi_extra={"x-aperture-labs-portal": "blue"})
async def read_items():
    return [{"item_id": "portal-gun"}]
```

If you open the automatic API docs, your extension will show up at the bottom of the specific path operation. [https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/path-operation-advanced-configuration/]

The resulting `/openapi.json` will include your extension field directly inside the operation object:

```json
{
    "openapi": "3.1.0",
    "info": { "title": "FastAPI", "version": "0.1.0" },
    "paths": {
        "/items/": {
            "get": {
                "summary": "Read Items",
                "operationId": "read_items_items__get",
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "Successful Response",
                        "content": { "application/json": { "schema": {} } }
                    }
                },
                "x-aperture-labs-portal": "blue"   // <-- your extension
            }
        }
    }
}
```
[https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/path-operation-advanced-configuration/]

---

### Advanced Use: Deep Merging with the Auto-Generated Schema

The dictionary in `openapi_extra` will be **deeply merged** with the automatically generated OpenAPI schema for the path operation. [https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/path-operation-advanced-configuration/] This means you can also use it to add or override other parts of the schema, such as a custom `requestBody`:

```python
from fastapi import FastAPI, Request

app = FastAPI()

@app.post(
    "/items/",
    openapi_extra={
        "requestBody": {
            "content": {
                "application/json": {
                    "schema": {
                        "required": ["name", "price"],
                        "type": "object",
                        "properties": {
                            "name": {"type": "string"},
                            "price": {"type": "number"},
                            "description": {"type": "string"},
                        },
                    }
                }
            },
            "required": True,
        },
    },
)
async def create_item(request: Request):
    raw_body = await request.body()
    return {"size": len(raw_body)}
```
[https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/path-operation-advanced-configuration/]

---

### Key Points to Remember

| Feature | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Parameter name** | `openapi_extra` on the path operation decorator |
| **Extension naming** | Must be prefixed with `x-` per the OpenAPI spec |
| **Merging behavior** | Deep-merged with the auto-generated schema |
| **Visibility** | Shows up in `/openapi.json` and the interactive docs UI |
| **Scope** | Applies only to the specific path operation it's declared on |

> 💡 **Tip:** This is a low-level extension point. If you only need to declare additional responses, a more convenient way is to use [https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/additional-responses/]. [https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/path-operation-advanced-configuration/]

