The `__init__` method of the `FixedContentQueryChecker` class accepts a single parameter: **`fixed_content`** of type `str`. [https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/advanced-dependencies/]

Here is the relevant code:

```python
class FixedContentQueryChecker:
    def __init__(self, fixed_content: str):
        self.fixed_content = fixed_content

    def __call__(self, q: str = ""):
        if q:
            return self.fixed_content in q
        return False
```

This parameter is used to "parameterize" the dependency — the value passed to `fixed_content` is stored as an instance attribute (`self.fixed_content`) and later used in the `__call__` method to check whether that fixed content string is present in a query. [https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/advanced-dependencies/]

For example, when creating an instance with `FixedContentQueryChecker("bar")`, the string `"bar"` is passed as `fixed_content` and stored inside the instance as `checker.fixed_content`. [https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/advanced-dependencies/]

